 We are looking for a dedicated Junior Network Engineer to join our team in Bucharest, Romania!
 About the job:
 We are seeking an motivated Network Administrator to manage and maintain EveryMatrix’s network infrastructure alongside our current team. The ideal candidate will have understanding of networking technologies, problem-solving abilities, and open to evolve its skills on enterprise level network. The Network Administrator role is to ensure the stability, security, and performance of our infrastructure, both on-premises and cloud-based.
 What You'll get to do:
The Network Engineer will be responsible of managing and maintaining Everymatrix’s enterprise network infrastructure.
Assist in acquiring, install and upgrade of IT components, licensing and software, and manages inventory: switches, routers, firewalls, access points;
Provides basic technical support for VPN solutions: site-to-site, remote access, IPSEC and SSL;
Network Maintenance: make sure all equipment is monitored, alerts are being sent, documentation is up to date;
Provides technical support for network security and monitoring solutions;
Support internal teams to handle network problems;
Troubleshoot network related problems in a timely manner;
Effectively communicate with the team members, peers and management;
Manage operational tasks and assure they are done within agreed SLAs;
Adhere to business standards and processes
Troubleshoot network team incidents and participate in elaborating a clear root cause analysis and complete mitigation plan;
Coordinate with all parties(clients, peers, vendors etc.) to ensure seamless operations and projects delivery;
Responsible for network devices lifecycle management and patch management;
Ensure accurate monitoring of network devices;
Ensures knowledge transfer from team engineers;
Other requirements raised by management;
 What we’re looking for:
Nice to have: Bachelor's degree in technical field(engineering, mathematics, IT);
Minimum of 1 years of technical background with various network equipment (routers, switches, firewalls);
Knowledge of routing, switching and network protocols (DHCP, ARP, dot1q, OSPF, BGP);
Knowledge of configuring and managing VPN solutions(site-to-site, Remote access, IPSEC, SSL);
Knowledge of managing firewall devices;
Knowledge of Linux OS and microservices;
Understanding of ITIL processes (certification is a plus);
Fluency in English, both written & spoken;
Good communication skills;
Analytical and research skills;
Problem-solving skills;
Ability to accept and adjust to changes – agile;
Oriented to details; 
Passionate about technology;
 Here's what we offer:
Start with 22 days of annual leave, with 2 additional days added each year, up to 32 days by your fifth year with us.
Hybrid work schedule is available after the first three months of employment, with up to 50 days of work from home per year.
Benefit from two Free Fridays each year, limited to one per quarter.
3 sick leave days per year, no doctor's note required.
Daily catered lunch or monthly lunch allowance.
Private Medical Subscription.
Access online learning platforms like Udemy for Business and LinkedIn Learning, and a budget for external training.
Access to an Employee Assistance Program through TELUS Health.
 Our office perks include parking, on-site massages, and frequent team-building activities in various locations. And did we mention our amazing office space complete with its own pool and gym?
At EveryMatrix, we're committed to creating a supportive and inclusive workplace where you can thrive both personally and professionally. Come join us and experience the difference!
